<p>Kazakhstan held a national referendum on March 15, and voters backed a new constitution, according to exit polls and early reporting from multiple outlets. The overhaul would bring broad political changes, but critics cited in several reports said it could strengthen presidential authority and potentially give President Kassym-Jomart Tokayev a path to stay in power beyond 2029. The vote took place amid concerns about how open and fair the process was. RFE/RL reported journalist detentions and media restrictions during the referendum, and said the OSCE had also raised transparency concerns. The result points to a major institutional shift in a country with an important role in global energy and minerals markets, while renewing scrutiny of Kazakhstan&#x27;s political system and civil liberties.</p><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Kazakh critics: Critics said the proposed constitutional changes could concentrate more power in the presidency instead of balancing state institutions. (<a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/kazakhstan-controversial-constitutional-referendum-media-restrictions/33707171.html'>RFE/RL</a>)</li><li>OSCE: The organization raised concerns about the transparency of the referendum process during the vote. (<a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/kazakhstan-controversial-constitutional-referendum-media-restrictions/33707171.html'>RFE/RL</a>)</li><li>Straits Times reporting: Its coverage said the constitutional redesign could leave President Kassym-Jomart Tokayev with a path to remain in power beyond 2029. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/kazakhstan-approves-new-constitution-in-referendum-exit-polls-say'>The Straits Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/kazakhstan-approves-new-constitution-in-referendum-exit-polls-say'>Kazakhstan approves new constitution in referendum, exit polls say</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/kazakhstan-controversial-constitutional-referendum-media-restrictions/33707171.html'>Journalists Detained As Kazakhstan Holds Controversial Referendum</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/kazakhstan-voters-back-constitutional-overhaul-exit-polls-show/a-76372891'>Kazakhstan voters back constitutional overhaul, exit polls show</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/kazakhs-vote-new-constitution-referendum-sunday-2026-03-13/'>Kazakhstanis vote in a referendum to approve a new constitution.</a> - reuters.com</li></ul>